<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch unadjusted unemployment falls in April-June.</title>
<headline>Dutch unadjusted unemployment falls in April-June.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch non-seasonally adjusted unemployment fell to an average of 376,000 in April-June from 381,000 in March-May, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT NON-SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			  April-June 97   March-May 97  April-June 96</p>
<p> total number	   376,000	  381,000	  418,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    5.6		5.7		6.3</p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			  April-June 97   March-May 97  April-June 96</p>
<p> total number	   395,000	  385,000	  438,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    5.9		5.8		6.5</p>
<p>NOTES - Percentages are calculated in relation to average 1996 labour force (6.681 million). By international standards, the CBS uses a narrow definition of unemployment. Figures are compiled from job centre registrations and CBS survey.</p>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters before publication of the figures had expected a non-seasonally adjusted April-June unemployment figure of around 365,000 and a seasonally adjusted figure of around 383,000.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000</p>
